# Architecture

## Packages

- `packages/app` — Electron shell + Vue UI (Forge, Vite, Tailwind, shadcn-vue)
- `packages/runner` — Go binary `pipebox` (CI runner + public CLI)

## Do not

- Put act/log parsing in `packages/app` (not in Vue, preload, or main as a permanent home — main only spawns and forwards)
- Reinvent act; wrap the CLI and normalize output to NDJSON events
- Expose a generic shell API through preload
- Build ad-hoc UI primitives; use shadcn-vue under `packages/app/src/components/ui/`
- After `shadcn-vue add`, rename generated Vue files to **kebab-case** (`Button.vue` → `button.vue`) and fix local imports — CLI defaults to PascalCase
- Add shadcn components only when a screen needs them (currently: `button`, `menubar`)

## Process boundaries

- **Renderer:** typed runner events + shadcn-vue only
- **Preload:** narrow typed bridge
- **Main:** spawn/kill `pipebox`, forward NDJSON → IPC, OS keychain secrets, file dialogs
- **Runner (`pipebox`):** discover workflows, run **Dockerized act** (`ghcr.io/nektos/act`), parse streams, emit events; CLI commands `doctor`, `list`, `run`, `install`
- **v1 dependency:** Docker only — do not require a local `act` binary

## Runner protocol (v1)

Stdout is NDJSON (one object per line): `workflow_list`, `run_started`, `run_finished`, `step_started`, `step_finished`, `log`, `error`.

Mirror types in the app at `packages/app/src/shared/runner-events.ts` (types-only copy of Go structs).
